          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पकावणो (pakāvṇo) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from pakva, \"cooked, ripe\". CDIAL lists Old Marwari pākaï under it (CDIAL 7621). The Old Marwari row means \"becomes ripe\"; पकावणो (pakāvṇo) is its causing form, \"make cooked\". The root is pac, \"to cook\"."
            }
          ]
        },
